From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:03:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] venus: on 9front a driver started again is found (gpuagain
 before the renderer looks for /dev/gpu/0)

A GPU's driver killed and started again (gpu(4)) posts /srv/gpu.0 anew
and mounts itself in the name space it was started in only; a program
whose name space has the mount of the dead one (the window system and
what it started) found no device: "no physical device" after the
device was lost. vn_renderer_create_plan9 calls gpuagain(0) (the tree's
plan9/lib/gpuagain.c), which mounts /srv/gpu.0 before /dev when
/dev/gpu/0 is dead.
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_plan9.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_plan9.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_plan9.c
index d08020a..f308db8 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_plan9.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_plan9.c
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@ extern void *segattach(int, char *, void *, unsigned long);
 extern int plan9_dmabuf_fd(const char *token);
 extern int plan9_dmabuf_token(int fd, char *buf, int n);
 extern int segdetach(void *);
+/* plan9/lib/gpuagain.c: /dev/gpu/n again after its driver started anew */
+extern int gpuagain(int n);
 
 #define PLAN9_GPU_DIR "/dev/gpu/0"
 #define PLAN9_PCI_VENDOR_ID 0x1af4
@@ -927,6 +929,11 @@ vn_renderer_create_plan9(struct vn_instance *instance,
    p9->submit_fd = -1;
    p9->fence_fd = -1;
 
+   /* a driver killed and started again (gpu(4)): its files over the dead
+    * ones in this name space, before they are looked for
+    */
+   gpuagain(0);
+
    VkResult result = plan9_init(p9);
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS) {
       plan9_destroy(&p9->base, alloc);
